{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00674",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 1.31,
      "end_seconds": 13.62,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "Doctor, I'll be direct, because I'm at the end of my rope. Walter has been up wandering the house at night, and I'm not sleeping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.07,
      "end_seconds": 23.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "I'm sorry to hear it. Walter, what do you make of it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.58,
      "end_seconds": 34.98,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "I get up for a stretch, that's all. It's been a week, one week, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 37.65,
      "end_seconds": 45.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "It's three weeks, Walter. I've counted. The first night was the Thursday after his birthday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.6,
      "end_seconds": 63.71,
      "duration_seconds": 15.11,
      "text": "So, one week from your side, three from Mrs Pearce's side. I'll write that down as one to three weeks. What does he do when he's up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 66.96,
      "end_seconds": 79.53,
      "duration_seconds": 12.57,
      "text": "He goes to the front door and tries the handle. Or he goes into the kitchen and opens every cupboard."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.79,
      "end_seconds": 86.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "I'm looking for something. I forget what."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.13,
      "end_seconds": 94.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Has he had any falls on his night walks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 95.76,
      "end_seconds": 101.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "No falls. He's steady, I always hear him and go down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.7,
      "end_seconds": 109.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Is there anyone in the family with memory trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 112.27,
      "end_seconds": 117.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "His mother had it, in her eighties. Walter's seventy-nine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.15,
      "end_seconds": 125.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "I see. Walter, can you walk across the room for me? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.12,
      "end_seconds": 146.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.0,
      "end_seconds": 155.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "He walks steadily, turns well, and doesn't need to hold on to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 158.38,
      "end_seconds": 164.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "That's him in the day. It's the night that's the trouble. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.31,
      "end_seconds": 175.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "It often is. Evenings and nights are hard for people whose memory is changing. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 177.05,
      "end_seconds": 180.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "What can I do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.81,
      "end_seconds": 195.7,
      "duration_seconds": 12.89,
      "text": "A few practical things. Keep the house well lit at night, with a lamp in the hall and the bathroom, and keep a regular bedtime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 198.12,
      "end_seconds": 204.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "We have a regular bedtime. It's the three o'clock wanders. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.53,
      "end_seconds": 219.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.83,
      "text": "Then a simple alarm on the front door, a bell or a chime, so you wake when he tries it. And lock away anything unsafe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 221.99,
      "end_seconds": 225.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I can get a chime. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.99,
      "end_seconds": 232.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Walter, do you nap in the day? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.31,
      "end_seconds": 238.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "A bit. After lunch. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.39,
      "end_seconds": 248.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Try keeping the naps short, and get some daylight and a walk in the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 250.91,
      "end_seconds": 253.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "He'd like that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.66,
      "end_seconds": 272.24,
      "duration_seconds": 15.58,
      "text": "Mrs Pearce, you need support as well. I'm going to refer you both to the community team for older people, who can talk about respite and what's available."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 275.29,
      "end_seconds": 280.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Thank you. I've been afraid to ask. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.94,
      "end_seconds": 285.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Please don't be. Ring us anytime. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 287.77,
      "end_seconds": 289.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.47,
      "end_seconds": 297.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "I'd like to help her sleep better, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.82,
      "end_seconds": 305.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Then you're both doing the right thing by coming in. ~"
    }
  ]
}
